---
description: Verify new HTML/CSS is legible in both light and dark modes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Light and dark mode contrast

The site theme is controlled by `color-mode` on `:root` (`light` | `dark`), not by `prefers-color-scheme` alone. New UI must be legible in **both** modes before the task is done.

## Use AP theme tokens

Prefer tokens from `src/index.css` that switch with `color-mode`:

- Backgrounds: `--main-bg-color`, `--secondary-color-3-bg`, `--tag-background-color`
- Text: `--main-font-color`, `--secondary-font-color`, `--main-heading-color`
- Accents / buttons: `--secondary-color-3`, `--secondary-color-3-lighter`, `--secondary-color-1`
- Shadows / borders: `--tag-background-color`, `--dropshadow-target-start`

```css
/* ❌ BAD — hardcoded or Bulma scheme vars */
.panel { background: white; color: #333; }
.widget { background: var(--bulma-scheme-main); }

/* ✅ GOOD — AP tokens follow color-mode */
.panel {
  background: var(--main-bg-color);
  color: var(--main-font-color);
  border: 1px solid var(--tag-background-color);
}
```

## Avoid Bulma scheme for themed surfaces

Bulma `--bulma-scheme-*` follows `prefers-color-scheme`, which can disagree with `color-mode`. Do not use Bulma scheme variables for backgrounds, text, or borders on custom UI. Use AP tokens or existing helpers (`.apButton`, `.apButtonNeutral`, `.table`).

## Button and hover states

Define **both** default and `:hover` / `:focus-visible` colors. Do not rely on global rules that set `--high-contrast-font-color` (white in light mode) without a contrasting background.

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
.btn-neutral {
  background: var(--main-bg-color);
  color: var(--main-font-color);
}
.btn-neutral:hover,
.btn-neutral:focus-visible {
  background: var(--tag-background-color);
  color: var(--main-font-color);
}
```

## React / inline styles

Avoid fixed hex colors for text or backgrounds in JSX unless they are board/game colours. Use `className` + CSS variables instead.

## Before finishing UI work

1. Mentally check (or describe checking) the change in **light** and **dark** mode.
2. Confirm text, borders, icons, and disabled/hover/selected states are readable on their backgrounds.
3. Confirm layered elements (headings with `.lined`, sticky docks, fixed panels) use matching background tokens so boxes do not “float” in the wrong colour.

If you cannot verify in a browser, say so and call out what should be checked manually.
